{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you to Target for supporting PBS."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2760,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pin-pricks in the celestial sphere, through\nwhich shines the light of heaven?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6959,
    "dDurationMs": 3881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or gods and heroes looking down from their\nconstellations?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10840,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or lights kindled above middle earth by Varda\nElbereth and brightened with the dew of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15250,
    "dDurationMs": 2039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trees of Valinor?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17289,
    "dDurationMs": 3141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Science has long pondered the mysteries of\nthe stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20430,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is how we finally figured them out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28480,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first thing you learn in astronomy is\nthat the sun and the other stars are giant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32590,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "balls of fiery hydrogen and helium, powered\nby raging nuclear furnaces in their cores."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37470,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this knowledge is surprisingly recent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39060,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A hundred years ago, we were starting to plumb\nthe deepest mysteries of the universe with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44780,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein’s relativity and with quantum theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But\nwe had no idea what that giant bright thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50040,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the sky was."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51700,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We didn’t know what stars were made of nor\nwhere their energy came from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56270,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, it’s impressive that\nwe figured it out at all - afterall, we’ve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61170,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "never been to a star, never sampled its stuff\nto put under a microscope."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65460,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet in a handful of years during the 1920s\nwe went from no idea to having a pretty solid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71520,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understanding of stellar physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73070,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a lot of it was thanks to a brilliant\nyoung astronomer named Cecilia Payne."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78820,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You may not have heard of Cecilia Payne - later\nCecilia Payne-Gaposchkin - and that’s a shame."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84460,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She not only revolutionized our understanding\nof the stars, but she helped blaze a trail"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88640,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in astronomy and physics for the women who\nwould come after."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91780,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’ll get to the physics in a minute - but\nPayne deserves a quick bio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97800,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She was born in Great Britain in 1900 and\nalways knew she wanted to be a scientist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103170,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She was tending towards biology at Cambridge\nUniversity where she ended up in a lecture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108610,
    "dDurationMs": 6570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the great astrophysicist Sir Arthur Eddington,\nwho recounted his recent solar eclipse expedition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115180,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which he verified Einstein’s new general\ntheory of relativity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119090,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Payne’s own words: “The result was\na complete transformation of my world picture.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125150,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She switched from biology to physics, finished\nher studies, but couldn’t even graduate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130190,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "properly - Cambridge simply did not award\nsuch degrees to women."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134880,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cecilia Payne set her eyes on the New World."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138130,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Harvard University in Massachusetts was already\nproving itself at least a little friendlier"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142810,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to women."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144190,
    "dDurationMs": 4879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Annie Jump Cannon and Henrietta Swan Leavitt\n- two of the greats of stellar astronomy - had"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149069,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come through Radcliffe College - the women’s\ncollege adjoining the all-male Harvard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154209,
    "dDurationMs": 4871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Harvard itself was just now opening its\ndoors to female graduate students."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159080,
    "dDurationMs": 6410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was 1923, and just out of her degree\nPayne was already extremely broadly knowledgeable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165490,
    "dDurationMs": 5630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Enough so that she knew what she wanted to\nresearch - she wanted to unlock the mysteries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171120,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172970,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’ll come back to Cecilia - for now let’s\nget to some stellar science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177530,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The secret to understanding the stars is not\nexactly in the light they send to us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182780,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rather, it’s in the light that they fail\nto send."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186569,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a modern spectrum of the Sun - it’s\nthe amount of light we receive at different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190819,
    "dDurationMs": 5161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "colors - or in other words, from photons of\ndifferent energies of frequencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195980,
    "dDurationMs": 5229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of this light comes the photosphere - a\nlayer around 100 km deep at the surface of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201209,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202209,
    "dDurationMs": 4731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s the glow of the 6000 K hot material\nin that layer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206940,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The colour of a star depends on that temperature\n- blue for hot stars, red for cooler stars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212550,
    "dDurationMs": 2729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sort of greenish-yellow for stars like\nour Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215279,
    "dDurationMs": 5141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But on its own, that thermal light is a very\nsmooth curve across the spectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220420,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what about these dark bands?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224240,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those are where photons of very specific energies\nhave been plucked out of this thermal light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230270,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It works like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231790,
    "dDurationMs": 4699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A photon trying to escape from inside the\nSun encounters a lot of obstacles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236489,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the most severe is that the Sun is\nfull of free electrons - electrons that were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240709,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stripped from their atoms due to the intense\nheat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243920,
    "dDurationMs": 3099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Electrons deflect the path of a photon very\neasily."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247019,
    "dDurationMs": 4271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So any given photon has to bounce its way\nbetween many electrons before finding its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251290,
    "dDurationMs": 1559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way to the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252849,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A photon coming from the core of the Sun will\nbe or scattered so many times that what should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257379,
    "dDurationMs": 4681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be a 1-second journey to the surface can take\n10s of thousands of years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262060,
    "dDurationMs": 4579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once it gets close to the surface, material\nis much less dense, so there are fewer free"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266639,
    "dDurationMs": 2231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electrons to do the scattering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268870,
    "dDurationMs": 4609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the time a photon reaches the photosphere\nit has a 50-50 chance of traveling the final"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273479,
    "dDurationMs": 2881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "100km to space without bumping into anything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276360,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At least, that’s true for most of the light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279270,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But some photons encounter a new obstacle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282520,
    "dDurationMs": 5139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As temperature drops, it becomes possible\nfor some electrons to be captured by nuclei"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287659,
    "dDurationMs": 1641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to form atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289300,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if free electrons are good at stopping\nphotons in their tracks, these atoms are even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293860,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294860,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An atom can absorb a photon if doing so would\ncause one of its electrons to jump up to a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300200,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher energy level."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302119,
    "dDurationMs": 5151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The energy of the photon and the energy of\nthe electron jump have to be exactly the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307270,
    "dDurationMs": 5039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So any photons trying to escape the Sun that\nhappen to have one of these particular energies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312309,
    "dDurationMs": 3451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are going to get sucked up on its way out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315880,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that’s what these dark lines are - we\ncall them absorption lines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319990,
    "dDurationMs": 3979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each element on the periodic table produces\na different set of lines corresponding to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323969,
    "dDurationMs": 2331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its unique energy levels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326300,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just seeing which absorption lines are present\ntells you which elements are present inside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330969,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332539,
    "dDurationMs": 4621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the spectrum of the Sun was first studied,\nit was noticed that the most prominent lines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337160,
    "dDurationMs": 3969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "corresponded to the most common elements on\nthe surface of the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341129,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The prevailing wisdom came to be that the\nsun was made of exactly the same stuff as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346089,
    "dDurationMs": 2651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Earth - just a lot, lot hotter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348740,
    "dDurationMs": 5690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to test this - to figure out the true\ncomposition of the sun from these absorption"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354430,
    "dDurationMs": 7010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lines - was going to take some serious advances\nin understanding how both stars and atoms work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361440,
    "dDurationMs": 2679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fortunately help was at hand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364119,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The brand new field of quantum mechanics was\nemerging in Europe, and a young astrophysicist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369319,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "named Cecilia Payne had just arrived at Harvard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373569,
    "dDurationMs": 4861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even that early in her career, Payne was widely\nread and so she knew about some groundbreaking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378430,
    "dDurationMs": 5799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work in early quantum theory that she could\nuse to decode the complex patterns of absorption"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384229,
    "dDurationMs": 1351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lines in stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385580,
    "dDurationMs": 4399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the reasons for the complexity of stellar\nspectra is that you don’t just get one pattern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389979,
    "dDurationMs": 2451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of absorption lines per element."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392430,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You get a different pattern for every different\nionization state of every different element."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398310,
    "dDurationMs": 5309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In energetic environments like the Sun, electrons\nare regularly kicked free from their atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403619,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The atoms are ionized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405749,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That changes the energy levels of the electrons\nthat remain, resulting in a different set"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409339,
    "dDurationMs": 3271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of possible absorption lines depending on\nhow many electrons have been kicked free."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412610,
    "dDurationMs": 4389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the pattern of absorption lines depends\non the abundance of each element AND on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416999,
    "dDurationMs": 3581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "abundance of each ionization state of that\nelement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420580,
    "dDurationMs": 5839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not long before Celilia Payne started her\nresearch, Indian astrophysicist Meghdad Saha"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426419,
    "dDurationMs": 4351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had used early ideas in quantum theory to\ncrack the ionization problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430770,
    "dDurationMs": 4859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He figured out a formula that told how much\nof each ionization state you should get if"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435629,
    "dDurationMs": 3391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have a cloud of some element at a given\ntemperature and pressure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439020,
    "dDurationMs": 5109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Saha and others began to apply this theory\nto stellar absorption lines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444129,
    "dDurationMs": 3271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it was Cecilia Payne to figured it all\nout."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447400,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Payne realized that it should be possible\nto translate a star’s absorption line pattern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450680,
    "dDurationMs": 2409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into measures of temperature and composition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453089,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it wasn’t straightforward - there are\nmultiple competing influences determining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456449,
    "dDurationMs": 2421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the strength of a given absorption line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458870,
    "dDurationMs": 4569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For one thing, each absorption line is formed\nas light deeper within the sun traverses a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463439,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "large distance, over which temperature and\npressure drop dramatically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466849,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And different lines are predominantly formed\nat different depths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469999,
    "dDurationMs": 4061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In astrophysics, these sort of messy, competing\neffects rule the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474060,
    "dDurationMs": 2789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s literally impossible to disentangle\neverything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476849,
    "dDurationMs": 6671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A big part of making progress in astrophysics\nis finding clean relationships amid the chaos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483520,
    "dDurationMs": 4579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cecilia realized a couple of things - first\nwas that although the strongest absorption"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488099,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lines were hard to interpret, theoretically\nthe strength of the weakest lines should be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492789,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "proportional to the abundance of the particular\nionization state of that element."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497209,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That didn’t tell you exactly how much of\nthat ion type there was - just the relative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502469,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amount compared to other ion types."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504369,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the second realization was that although\nshe couldn’t get the total quantity of each"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509069,
    "dDurationMs": 5711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ion or of the element, with certain assumptions\nshe could get the relative amounts of the elements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514780,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compared to each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516250,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cecilia Payne set about analyzing the many\nspectra of stars that had been observed at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521680,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Harvard Observatory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523660,
    "dDurationMs": 5830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She calculated the relative abundances of\nthe elements and found they varied between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529490,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stars, but were generally similar to what\nwe find on Earth’s surface - but with a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534370,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "couple of extreme differences."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536300,
    "dDurationMs": 7140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On Earth, hydrogen is the third most abundant\nelement after oxygen and silicon, while helium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543440,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is extremely rare."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545100,
    "dDurationMs": 6270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Her results suggested that hydrogen was by\nfar the most common atom in the sun, followed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551370,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "closely by helium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553510,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cecilia Payne had discovered what the sun\nand stars were made of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was totally against the current scientific\nconsensus - which was that the Sun was made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563760,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the same stuff as the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565620,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Payne was advised to downplay that result\nin her thesis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569070,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She glossed over the result, saying that it\nwas “almost certainly not real” - that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573470,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was likely the result of not understanding\nthe atomic theory of hydrogen and helium well"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577780,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579040,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the fact of the sun being made mostly\nof hydrogen and helium was confirmed only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584300,
    "dDurationMs": 6260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few years later, and Cecilia Payne is widely\nrecognized for discovering this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590560,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the way, the whole finding out what stars\nare made of thing wasn’t even the main point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595220,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Payne’s thesis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596980,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She also developed a way to calculate the\ntemperatures of stars just based on the absorption"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601790,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602790,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was much more precise than the previous\nmethod of just observing the overall color"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607730,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the thermal light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608870,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, yeah, that’s how we know what the stars\nare made of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613210,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At around the same time as Ceclia Payne was doing all of this, other scientists were figuring out the rest of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618470,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mysteries of the stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620200,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Arthur Eddington himself had postulated the\nwhole nuclear fusion thing just a few years earlier"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624700,
    "dDurationMs": 6180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1920, but now knowing what stars are made\nof, he and others were able to develop a detailed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630880,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "theory of stellar physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633140,
    "dDurationMs": 4861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stars went from being utterly mysterious to\none of the best-understood denizens of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638001,
    "dDurationMs": 1599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639600,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And Cecilia?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640800,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She stayed in the US and became the first\nfemale professor at Harvard, and the first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645200,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "female chair of one of its departments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646980,
    "dDurationMs": 7410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, here’s to the stars - both types - Cecilia\nPayne-Gaposchkin, star astrophysicist, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654390,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also the type she figured out for us - the\ngiant balls of burning hydrogen scattered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658870,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across space time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660800,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today's episode was part of PBS's American\nPortrait Series."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664490,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We know we have a very international audience,\nbut for those of you within the USA, PBS is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669420,
    "dDurationMs": 5670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "asking you to share your stories, experiences\nand ideas on your life in America today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675090,
    "dDurationMs": 5571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "PBS American Portrait is a nationwide storytelling\nproject — a chance to be seen, heard, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680661,
    "dDurationMs": 2749,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to give a glimpse into your own life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683410,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everyone has a story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684410,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Share yours at:pbs.org/americanportrait."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688000,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’d like to thank Target for being a proud\nsupporter of PBS."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691410,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since the first Target opened in 1962, their\nmission has been to help families discover"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695530,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the joy of everyday life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697010,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In all 50 states, Target is dedicated to being\na good neighbor, and working with their communities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701420,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and partners to make life a little better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703990,
    "dDurationMs": 5410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are over 350,000 team-members employed\nby Target to continue their mission every day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709400,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To learn more about Target’s commitments,\nyou can check out target.com/community or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714320,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "click the link in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716540,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we’re going to have to skip comment responses\nfor a week due to some travels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719750,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’ll do double comments next week."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722110,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I do want to take this opportunity to\nsend a big, big thank you to one of our Patreon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727080,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supporters, Mark Rosenthal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729710,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mark supports us at the big bang level - which\nbasically means we get to film the show, animate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735370,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it, AND each lunch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737500,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mark, we've talked about a lot of stars today, so it’s fitting we end on you, the starriest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743060,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "star of all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744450,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks for helping us to .... shoot for the\nstars?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
